course: dictionary
lesson: 47
title: Agreements and "according to"
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An accord is a fancy word for an agreement, a promise that two sides make together. When two countries agree to stop fighting, they sign a peace accord. Look for the clues around the word: the words «signed» and «peace» tell you it is an agreement.
explain: Some phrases use accord in a short, special way. «He tidied his room of his own accord.» Nobody asked him, so "of his own accord" must mean by his own choice. Try your meaning in the sentence: "He tidied his room by his own choice" still makes sense.
explain: «According to» is a phrase you will meet all the time. «According to my friends, I am not very clever» means "as my friends say". «According to the table, Sam scored 12 points» means "as the table shows". Swap in "as said by" or "as shown by", and if it still makes sense, you have found the meaning.
fact: An accord is an official agreement, often between countries or groups.
fact: «Of your own accord» means by your own choice, without being told.
fact: «In accord with» means agreeing with or matching something.
fact: «According to» means as said by someone or as shown by something.
fact: In formal writing, accord can be a verb: to accord someone respect means to give them respect.
exercise: «The two countries signed a peace accord.» What is an accord? | A type of musical instrument | A loud noise | *An official agreement | A fight between two teams
exercise: «Mia cleaned the kitchen of her own accord.» What does this phrase tell you? | She was paid to do it | *She chose to do it without being asked | She was told to do it by her teacher | She broke the window
exercise: Toad says, «I'm not really clever, according to my friends.» What does according to mean here? | Against | Before | *As said by
test: «The map showed the path, according to the old book.» What does according to mean? | Wrongly, by mistake | *As shown by | Far away from | After
test: Which phrase means agreeing with or matching something? | According to | *In accord with | Peace accord | Of your own accord
exam: In «The team played according to the rules», what does according to mean? | Instead of | Without | Against | *Following
